designeleases\0_1_0\F_145_action_popup_on_mobile.md:16:On mobile, when an action popup is opened, show it as max screen, like the card popup
designeleases\0_1_0\F_145_action_popup_on_mobile.md:20:- Every action popup uses `ResizablePopper` with an initial 400 × 450 size, an anchor position, drag and resize controls, and a stored desktop size.
designeleases\0_1_0\F_145_action_popup_on_mobile.md:22:- Mobile card details already use a full-screen layout, but action popups keep their desktop layout and can exceed the usable mobile viewport.
designeleases\0_1_0\F_145_action_popup_on_mobile.md:26:- Detect mobile inside the shared action-popup path with the existing `theme.breakpoints.down('md')` breakpoint. Apply the result to every card, file, folder, and project action popup, including search and project-agent entry points.
designeleases\0_1_0\F_145_action_popup_on_mobile.md:34:- When any action popup opens at the mobile breakpoint, it fills the viewport from its top-left corner without margins or rounded corners.
designeleases\0_1_0\F_142_improve_board_view_on_mobile.md:40:- Keep `Run` button as action-popup entry; long-press must not open card actions.
designeleases\0_1_0\F_140_persist_conversation_view_state.md:107:- Events: only exact card/action popup subscribers and the affected card aggregate subscriber update; no card snapshot refresh occurs.
designeleases\0_1_0\F_138_reduce_action_popup_rerenders_during_streaming.md:4:title: reduce action popup rerenders during streaming
designeleases\0_1_0\F_138_reduce_action_popup_rerenders_during_streaming.md:17:While an agent is producing a response, short text updates (streaming deltas) arrive very frequently. Each delta currently causes far more rendering work in the action popup than necessary. The deltas themselves are wanted (text should appear as soon as possible); the problem is how much re-renders per delta.
designeleases\0_0_3\F_84_select_empty_conversation.md:16:After selecting a conversation in the dropdown on an action popup, it is no longer possible to get out of the conversation history. you can select another historical conv, but not an empty one. User needs to be able to select an empty conversation again (top item shouldn't be disabled)
designeleases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:3:title: Select workTree from action popup
designeleases\0_0_3\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:14:User can select the active worktree from the action popup. When the action popup is associated to a card, it reflects the worktree of that card (and also updates it). When the action popup is for the project agent, then the user can select the worktree on which to run the agent project wide.
designeleases\0_0_3\F_82_waitforinput_state_display.md:17:When a streaming-agent goes into 'WaitForInput' state, the card action button and buttons on the action popup should no longer show 'running' state, but 'waitForInput' state so that the user knows he needs to look at the card.
designeleases\0_1_0\F_125_show_waitforinput_state_when_agent_asked_question.md:20:`ActionRun` publishes structured questions and approval requests as `update` events with status `waitingForInput`. `ActionRunRegistry` stores their payloads but does not apply that status to the live run. `CardRunButton` and `ActionSelector` therefore keep showing `running`, because live run status overrides persisted conversation status.
designeleases\0_1_0\F_113_only_show_responses_when_in_waitforinput_mode.md:23:Response prompts are the selected action's `phrases`. `ActionPhraseButtonsOwner` shows them for any agent follow-up: while the scoped run is queued, running, or `waitingForInput`, and after the run when a stored conversation can continue. Therefore they can appear as soon as a run starts and outside the period when the agent awaits user input.
designeleases\0_1_0\F_113_only_show_responses_when_in_waitforinput_mode.md:34:- Preserve phrase behavior: click replaces the current prompt draft; double-click replaces and submits it. Preserve button labels, order, keyboard access, and the `Predefined phrases` accessible group name.
designeleases\0_1_0\F_110_card_action_popup_should_show_card_id.md:5:title: card-action popup should show card id
designeleases\0_1_0\F_110_card_action_popup_should_show_card_id.md:16:currently it's rather hard to see which action-popup belongs to which card (or is for the global project agent).
designeleases\0_1_0\F_110_card_action_popup_should_show_card_id.md:34:- Every card action popup visibly shows its card ID in the header.
designeleases\0_1_0\F_106_active_popup_to_front.md:21:`CardActionPopupService` keeps one entry per open card action popup, and `CardActionPopupHost` renders them with stable ids. Every `ActionPopup` uses `ResizablePopper`, whose Popper root has the same modal z-index. Portal order therefore leaves the last opened popup above older popups, even after the user focuses or clicks an older one.
designeleases\0_1_0\F_106_active_popup_to_front.md:34:- Newly opened card action popup appears above existing card action popups.
designeleases\0_1_0\F_106_active_popup_to_front.md:35:- Clicking, dragging, resizing, or moving keyboard focus into a lower popup brings it above all other card action popups.
designeleases\0_1_0\F_105_add_color_to_action_button_for_waiting.md:17:When an agent-action is waiting for response of the user, on the action-popup, the action button shows a question mark icon in front of the action name on the button. this is ok, but to make it more clearly, we should show the button border in the same color as used for the 'run' button on the card.
